        "rationale": "The FIFO incorrectly accepts writes when full because `do_write` is not gated by the full condition. This causes the write pointer to advance and overwrite the oldest data, leading to wrong read data. The fix adds a check for `count != DEPTH` (i.e., not full) to `do_write`, ensuring writes are ignored when full as required by the contract.",
        "diff": "--- a/dut.v\n+++ b/dut.v\n@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@\n     reg [AW:0]      count;\n \n     wire do_read  = rd_en && (count != 0);\n-    wire do_write = wr_en;\n+    wire do_write = wr_en && (count != DEPTH);\n \n     assign empty = (count == 0);\n     assign full  = (count == DEPTH);\n",
        "candidate_run_id": "20261009-154833-ver-5bb770",
